WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Leonardo DiCaprio. You were one of the first people to work with him.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.020
How old was he in "This American boy"?

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.240
"This boy's life", pardon.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.160
Was he about 14 or 13 or 14?

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:11.980
Young.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.580
Young.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.984
It must be amazing to see, you know, to watch his career.

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:17.880
Yes. Yeah. Yeah

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.640
Leo was also - we had a reading of the movie and

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.559
Leo wasn't reading the lead. It was another kid and and at the end of it I said

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:31.289
"This kid is interesting, you know.

00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:34.559
You should che- you know, pay more attention to him."

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.200
And I don't know whether that

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.760
My saying that had anything to do with it, but that was-

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.240
You know it did.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.280
Anointed by Robert De Niro. Other kids. Who knows where they are now.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.760
Someone else though. Someone else had a huge influence on Leonardo DiCaprio's career. I turn to Paul Rudd.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.930
(laughs)

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.197
You did, though. You properly did.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.000
I don't know, I don't think I had an influence. But, I sometimes I, you know, looking back

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.440
find yourself in some interesting conversations and moments in time and

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.560
I worked with Leonardo on Romeo and Juliet.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.200
And at the time, my father

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.400
made his living. He was a Titanic expert and he used to take people all over the world

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.700
talking about Titanic. He could go to universities.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.500
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.260
It was my last day of filming

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:31.169
Romeo and Juliet and we all went out to a bar afterward. All the guys...

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.930
We were all a bunch of guys working on the movie

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:40.199
And so we were in different cars and I was riding to the place with Leo and he said, "I just got offered this movie

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:48.030
And it's a big movie". He had done indie films to that point. He said "it's a big, it's a studio movie. It's Titanic".

00:01:49.149 --> 00:01:53.099
And I said "That's incredible!" and I knew a lot about Titanic because my dad just talks about Titanic

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.600
And we just had a conversation about it and

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.449
He was saying like, "I don't know what I'll do". I remember saying: "You should do it!"

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:11.609
I don't think I had any say, but it is kind of interesting to think back on that.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.869
Yeah, there was a moment when he might never done it. -Yeah, cause he didn't. He didn't do the movie.

